  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "10.0.0: the first release of Solhigson.Admin, the admin kit: Razor components for Solhigson apps, rendered statically on the server, with no interactive render mode and no inline script; an app owns every route, and the package holds components and no screen yet. Head and theme: KitHead, first in <head>, links the kit's stylesheet and scripts with the page's nonce where its policy uses one; KitTheme reads the viewer's light or dark choice from its cookie on the server, with KitTheme.HtmlAttributes(HttpContext) for <html>, and KitThemeSwitch offers the choice. Components: KitButton, KitStatusPill and KitAlert; KitField, one field for every input kind; KitDialog (a modal or a drawer) and KitConfirm on the native <dialog>; KitMenu, KitMenuItem and KitMenuForm, a row menu on the native popover; KitShell, the admin layout with a skip link, a side rail, a top bar with the user's menu (the theme choices and sign-out) and the main region; KitPageHeader, KitLead, KitEmptyState and KitPager; KitTable with KitColumn, and KitFilterBar, Get or Post; KitMark; and KitGallery, every component in every state on fixed example data, for a page an app adds in development or behind a permission. Links: every url a kit component takes goes through KitHref: a ~/ path is joined to the path base; a button's or a link menu item's Href may also be an https:// address (KitHref.LocalOrHttps), and a form's action is local alone (KitHref.Local). Menu: IKitMenuSource builds the shell's menu from the permissions the signed-in user's roles hold, read through PermissionManager's cached reads, and AddSolhigsonAdmin<TUser, TContext>() or AddSolhigsonAdmin<TUser, TKey, TContext>() registers it; the menu shows, each page's [Permission] enforces. Styles: tokens for every colour, size, space, radius, shadow, duration, curve and font, light and dark, in layers (kit.tokens, kit.base, kit.components) that an app's app layer overrides, each name listed in kit.manifest.json, a name leaving which is a breaking change; every motion reads a duration token that is 0ms under prefers-reduced-motion. Rules: the package's tests hold its markup, scripts and stylesheets to no inline script, style or handler, no other host, every href and form action through KitHref, measured contrast pairs, and no colour, length or duration outside the tokens. Depends on Solhigson.Framework.Core 10.24.0 or later.",
